%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ea1fbb0ab59d4c84a59e909f29a5c4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: DontCallMe::DontCallMe.Data.DayData
  day: 2
  dateLabel: Wednesday, 7 October
  weekday: Wed
  shortLabel: "Day 2 \xB7 Wed 7 Oct"
  place: Mangwon-dong, Seoul
  startTime: 16:20
  intro: Rent day. You meant to send it to Mr. Choi after class, like every month.
  ringDelay: 7
  variants:
  - id: scam
    conversation: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 22f2aed7e321048b1abf80217b6a709b, type: 2}
    phone: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 70939c56e2207464b95a14904dfde186, type: 2}
    room: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e56ae609b70414623bb93ec08017ab05, type: 2}
    directory: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5e6ad6ff1111844828136268946bd8cd, type: 2}
    clues:
    - id: number
      text: 'The caller''s number isn''t the son''s: your lease gives 010-2280-6614,
        and CheckFirst shows the caller''s as a prepaid phone opened six days ago.'
      where: "Desk drawer \u2192 Lease contract, or Computer \u2192 Check a phone
        number"
      when:
      - kind: 1
        target: "Lease contract \xB7 Unit 302"
      - kind: 2
        target: 010-4127-8830
    - id: account_owner
      text: 'The "new rent account" is in a stranger''s name: SEO JIYEON.'
      where: "Computer \u2192 Check a bank account"
      when:
      - kind: 2
        target: 620-118-449027
      - kind: 3
        target: 620-118-449027
    - id: landlord
      text: 'Mr. Choi was writing in the residents'' chat this afternoon: at home,
        fixing a light, asking for the rent on the usual account.'
      where: "Chats \u2192 Mangwon Heights residents"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: villa
    papers:
    - outcome: 1
      headline: Fake "landlord's son" calls tenants on rent day
      subhead: The landlord was at home all along. Tenants who checked their lease
        kept their rent.
      body: 'A man claiming to be the son of a Mangwon-dong landlord phoned tenants
        on rent day yesterday. His father was in hospital, he said, and this month''s
        rent should go to a new account before 5 p.m.


        The real landlord,
        Choi Youngsik, 71, was not in hospital: he spent the afternoon organising
        a water tank cleaning. "My son''s number is in every lease," he said. "And
        the rent account only changes when I write it down."


        Police say
        the account the caller gave, Hanbit Bank 620-118-449027, belongs to a woman
        who sold her bank book online. Anyone called by 010-4127-8830 should report
        it to 112.'
      verdictNote: You hung up and kept the rent. The lease had the son's real number,
        and the chat showed Mr. Choi at home.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 8687e732fe83540049be292512a0ee15, type: 3}
    - outcome: 0
      headline: Tenant loses a month's rent to a fake landlord's son
      subhead: 450,000 won went to a stranger's account. The landlord never asked
        for it.
      body: 'A man claiming to be the son of a Mangwon-dong landlord phoned tenants
        on rent day yesterday. His father was in hospital, he said, and this month''s
        rent should go to a new account before 5 p.m.


        A 22-year-old student
        sent 450,000 won to Hanbit Bank 620-118-449027. The account belongs to a
        woman who sold her bank book online; the money was withdrawn within minutes.


        The
        real landlord, Choi Youngsik, 71, was not in hospital: he spent the afternoon
        organising a water tank cleaning. "My son''s number is in every lease," he
        said. "And the rent account only changes when I write it down."


        Police
        ask anyone called by 010-4127-8830 to report it to 112.'
      verdictNote: The account was in SEO JIYEON's name, and the caller's number
        wasn't the one in your lease.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 49aa448867e3f4df6b1d012b0cc41ae8, type: 3}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: 'Rent-day calls: "pay my new account"'
      subhead: Tenants in Mangwon kept their rent, but few reported the calls.
      body: 'A man claiming to be the son of a Mangwon-dong landlord phoned tenants
        on rent day yesterday. His father was in hospital, he said, and this month''s
        rent should go to a new account before 5 p.m.


        Most tenants let
        the call run on until the caller gave up. The real landlord, Choi Youngsik,
        71, was not in hospital: he spent the afternoon organising a water tank cleaning.
        "My son''s number is in every lease," he said. "And the rent account only
        changes when I write it down."


        Police ask anyone called by 010-4127-8830
        to report it to 112.'
      verdictNote: Nothing was sent, but you never decided. The lease and the residents'
        chat had the answer.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 021adfc04d8a5413a9a5da5672b99158, type: 3}
    ruleTitle: A new rent account? Check the lease
    rule: No reports doesn't mean safe. Check the caller's number and the account
      holder's name against your lease, and ask the landlord's own chat.
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 8 Oct
  - id: legit
    conversation: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b5782b6a4626142aeb0c45af35ce3eb5, type: 2}
    phone: {fileID: 11400000, guid: aa208c986f6b54834b6580dd0b9383d9, type: 2}
    room: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3060e3da6775b47c3aa5d4b1db8cbb4f, type: 2}
    directory: {fileID: 11400000, guid: baf3a0b530af9438c878caa3a20f573f, type: 2}
    clues:
    - id: number
      text: The caller's number, 010-2280-6614, is the son's number in your lease,
        registered to Choi Hyunwoo.
      where: "Desk drawer \u2192 Lease contract, or Computer \u2192 Check a phone
        number"
      when:
      - kind: 1
        target: "Lease contract \xB7 Unit 302"
      - kind: 2
        target: 010-2280-6614
    - id: account_owner
      text: The new account is in Choi Hyunwoo's name, the son your lease names.
      where: "Computer \u2192 Check a bank account"
      when:
      - kind: 2
        target: 110-771-202358
      - kind: 3
        target: 110-771-202358
    - id: landlord
      text: Mr. Choi wrote in the residents' chat this morning that he is in hospital
        and that Hyunwoo collects this month's rent on this account.
      where: "Chats \u2192 Mangwon Heights residents, or the calendar on the wall"
      when:
      - kind: 4
        target: villa
      - kind: 0
        target: Calendar
    papers:
    - outcome: 0
      headline: A son keeps the building running
      subhead: While Mangwon Heights' landlord recovers from surgery, his son collects
        the rent, after a message to every tenant.
      body: 'Choi Youngsik, 71, who owns Mangwon Heights on Poeun-ro, had knee surgery
        at Severance Hospital yesterday. While he recovers, his son Choi Hyunwoo
        is collecting the rent, and found out how hard that can be.


        "Dad
        wrote the new account in the residents'' chat before he went in," Hyunwoo
        said. "Some tenants checked everything before paying, which I was glad to
        see."


        The Seoul Housing Centre says tenants are right to check
        a new rent account against the lease, the landlord''s own message and the
        name on the account. "Checking works both ways," a spokesperson said. "When
        they all match, the change is real."'
      verdictNote: 'The change was real, and you checked it: the number in your lease,
        the name on the account and the landlord''s own message all matched.'
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: a365c11f6902c42c18a9663ba26ef4ca, type: 3}
    - outcome: 1
      headline: When the real call sounds like a scam
      subhead: A landlord's son says half the tenants hung up on him on rent day.
      body: 'Choi Youngsik, 71, who owns Mangwon Heights on Poeun-ro, had knee surgery
        at Severance Hospital yesterday. While he recovers, his son Choi Hyunwoo
        is collecting the rent, and found out how hard that can be.


        "After
        all the scam calls, I understand," Hyunwoo said. "But Dad wrote the new account
        in the chat that morning, and my number is in every lease. It was all there."


        The
        Seoul Housing Centre says tenants are right to check a new rent account against
        the lease, the landlord''s own message and the name on the account. "Checking
        works both ways," a spokesperson said. "When they all match, the change is
        real."'
      verdictNote: This one was real. The number in your lease, the landlord's own
        message and the name on the account all matched.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: f7f0d9c1827c9442887c7e9ac6bd2de8, type: 3}
    - outcome: 3
      headline: Rent day, hospital day
      subhead: A landlord's son waited on the line for tenants who never decided.
      body: 'Choi Youngsik, 71, who owns Mangwon Heights on Poeun-ro, had knee surgery
        at Severance Hospital yesterday. While he recovers, his son Choi Hyunwoo
        is collecting the rent, and found out how hard that can be.


        "I
        waited on the phone for ages," Hyunwoo said. "The chat message and the lease
        had everything they needed."


        The Seoul Housing Centre says tenants
        are right to check a new rent account against the lease, the landlord''s
        own message and the name on the account. "Checking works both ways," a spokesperson
        said. "When they all match, the change is real."'
      verdictNote: The change was real, and the evidence was in the lease, the chat
        and the account's name. Deciding in time matters too.
      print: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 69bd3651b164a42cb9b7db7ba31a28db, type: 3}
    ruleTitle: Checking works both ways
    rule: When the number in your lease, the landlord's own message and the name
      on the account all match, the change is real. Check, then act.
    ruleSource: Seoul Daily, 8 Oct
